    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Gunnar Henderson** headlining the roster as our premier option. With an elite efficiency score of 81.88, **Gunnar Henderson** benefits significantly from a favorable park factor and a strong platoon advantage against Will Warren, positioning him as the centerpiece of our attack. He is closely followed in projected output by **Jackson Merrill** (74.17) and **Kyle Tucker** (74.09), both of whom take advantage of excellent park conditions to maintain high-floor production. Meanwhile, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (73.66) and **Heliot Ramos** (69.03) find themselves in opportunistic spots against Chris Bassitt, with both players gaining substantial momentum from an impressive 19% boost related to the pitcher's skill profile, ensuring our middle infield and outfield anchors remain highly productive despite the high-stakes environment.\n\nThe most difficult bench decision involved **Luis Robert Jr.**, who barely missed the starting cut with a score of 52.26. While his raw talent is undeniable, the optimizer relegated **Luis Robert Jr.** to the bench due to a -15% drag caused by a dynamic platoon disadvantage against Michael King and concerns regarding King\u2019s ability to neutralize stolen base attempts, a critical factor for our team strategy. On the risk front, we are maintaining a watchful eye on **Liam Hicks**, **Drake Baldwin**, **Coby Mayo**, **Nasim Nunez**, **Jacob Wilson**, **Miguel Vargas**, **Andy Pages**, and **Sam Antonacci** as we await final lineup cards. While their current scores are calculated on assumed batting order positions, any shifts\u2014particularly for **Nasim Nunez**\u2014could impact his marginal score of 53.75. Furthermore, while **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** remains sidelined, his absence continues to necessitate a strategic reliance on our current active depth, particularly as we monitor **Dominic Smith** and **Wade Meckler** as potential mid-game pivots should the weather or official lineup confirmations necessitate a change in our tactical approach.",
